-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",438,{
[13985]="70037162\n1\tTalk to Thane Tordag in his encampment\tThane Tordag is at his encampment, north of the road between Torsbury and Stoke. Torferth instructed you to bring your report to his father, Thane Tordag.\n",
[13986]="7004A396\n1\tRepair elaborate gearworks\tElaborate gearworks can be found in Udûn, You should repair gearworks.\n2\tRepair elaborate gearworks (total: 9)\030Use crankshafts (total: 9)\tElaborate gearworks can be found in Udûn, You should repair gearworks.\n3\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[13987]="7003FAE9\n1\tFish up and defeat the turtles (total: 4)\tSwamps are north of Calembel, north-east of Dol Amroth. Torchuil asked you to go fishing for turtles in the swamps north of Calembel and to dispatch of any you caught.\n2\tSpeak to Torchuil\tTorchuil is in Dol Amroth. Torchuil will be pleased to know the turtles have been thinned.\n",
[13988]="7002D44C\n1\tTalk to Sig Mandrake\tMandrake's Finest Stews and Sauces can be found in the town of Bree, east of the Mud-gate, by the south-western fountain. You have read a posted notice desiring help with preparing a stew of some sort and should report to Sig Mandrake in his shop for the details.\n2\tCollect tiny turtles from the northern bank of Halecatch Lake (total: 6)\tTiny turtles can be found on the northern bank of Halecatch Lake, south of the village of Bree. Sig Mandrake has asked for your help collecting the very specific turtles he needs in order to make a large batch of soup for a hungry customer.\n3\tBring tiny turtles to Sig Mandrake in Bree\tSig Mandrake is at his shop in Bree, east of the Mud Gate, in the south-western section of town. You have gathered tiny turtles for Sig Mandrake and should bring them to him at his shop.\n",
[13989]="7005873C\n1\tDefeat mammoths upon the battlefield (total: 6)\tMammoths can be found upon the battlefield. You should defeat any mammoths you find upon the battlefield.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many mammoths upon the battlefield.\n",
[13990]="70027ACD\n1\tTalk to Tecwin to begin the journey past Wulf's Cleft\tTecwin is waiting for you in Durgors. Tecwin will accompany you to the east to inform the rest of the Boar-clan resistance what has happened.\n2\tTalk to Gwin above Wulf's Cleft\tGwin awaits you above Wulf's Cleft. Having narrowly escaped Wulf's Cleft with your life, you find yourself on the cliffs of Carreglyn with members of the Boar-clan by your side.\n",
[13991]="7002A674\n1\tRide Tecwin's Horse and then talk to Gwin\tGwin awaits you above Wulf's Cleft. Having travelled from Dunbog, you have arrived to find Gwin looking down at a large Dunlending army. Speak to Gwin to find out what happened here.\n",
[13992]="700261AB\n1\tReturn to your trainers and learn how to train your skills\tUglash has asked you to return to your trainers and learn more about what it takes to become a true soldier in the war against the Free Peoples. The trainers are back where you started your life as a Warg. Speak with Gruglok.\n2\tTalk to Zagfra, a Corruptor of Gramsfoot\tHaving spoken to Gruglok, you should now talk to the Corruptor to learn about traits.\n3\tTalk to Hoitgoth\tNow that you have (presumably) equipped some traits, speak with the Corruptions Trainer to learn more about Corruptions in Monster Play.\n4\tTalk to Uglash to finish the tutorial\tNow that you have learned how to best equip yourself in Monster Play, speak with Uglash again for final instructions.\n",
[13993]="70064475\n1\tTalk to Malavin\tWar-tyrant Akúlhun directed you to the war tent to speak with an Angmarim sorceress there named Malavin. Apparently she is here to assist, inspect, or guide the war effort. Whatever her purpose, it does not sit well with the War-tyrant.\n2\tSpeak with the emissaries\tMalavin instructed you to speak to each of the emissaries representing the clans of Carn Dûm and beyond. They have blessings that they will seek to bestow upon you, provided you will serve in their name.\n3\tTalk to Malavin\tHaving spoken to all the emissaries it is time to return to Malavin for further instruction.\n",
[13994]="7006455B\n1\tIntroduce yourself to Captain-General Tordúr\tMake your way from the fountain to the front of this encampment to the north. There you should meet Captain-General Tordúr who leads this expedition in the Ettenmoors.\n",
[13995]="70064474\n1\tChoose a clan and receive their blessing\tThe time has come to choose your clan allegiance. All you need do is speak with one of the emissaries and choose to represent them on the field of battle.\n2\tTalk to Malavin\tWith your choice of clan made, you should return to the emissary, Malavan and speak with her.\n",
[13996]="70064472\n1\tSpeak with Lingemil and learn about training skills\tLingemil is your trainer in the Ettenmoors. Speak with them and learn about skills in the Ettenmoors.\n2\tPurchase and use the skill March!\tLingemil instructed you to speak with them again and learn the skill March!. Then, you are to use the skill so that Lengemil can see that you understand how to use the new skill you earned.\n3\tSpeak with Lingemil\tYou successfully enabled the skill March!. Speak with Lingemil again to learn more.\n4\tSpeak with Nadar near the gate of Gramsfoot\tYou have learned to strengthen yourself and to move swiftly. Lingemil directed you to a vendor near the gate. Curious. Seek out the vendor Nadar and speak with them.\n",
[13997]="700644D6\n1\tSpeak with Gruglok and learn about training skills\tGruglok is your trainer in the Ettenmoors. Speak with them and learn about skills in the Ettenmoors.\n2\tPurchase and use the skill March!\tGruglok instructed you to speak with them again and learn the skill March!. Then, you are to use the skill so that Gruglok can see that you understand how to use the new skill you earned.\n3\tSpeak with Gruglok\tYou successfully enabled the skill March!. Speak with Gruglok again to learn more.\n4\tSpeak with Nadar near the gate of Gramsfoot\tYou have learned to strengthen yourself and to move swiftly. Gruglok directed you to a vendor near the gate. Curious. Seek out the vendor Nadar and speak with them.\n",
[13998]="700644DA\n1\tSpeak with Dagalúr and learn about training skills\tLingemil is your trainer in the Ettenmoors. Speak with them and learn about skills in the Ettenmoors.\n2\tPurchase and use the skill March!\tDagalúr instructed you to speak with them again and learn the skill March!. Then, you are to use the skill so that Dagalúr can see that you understand how to use the new skill you earned.\n3\tSpeak with Dagalúr\tYou successfully enabled the skill March!. Speak with Dagalúr again to learn more.\n4\tSpeak with Nadar near the gate of Gramsfoot\tYou have learned to strengthen yourself and to move swiftly. Dagalúr directed you to a vendor near the gate. Curious. Seek out the vendor Nadar and speak with them.\n",
[13999]="700644DB\n1\tSpeak with Sovairlë and learn about training skills\tSovairlë is your trainer in the Ettenmoors. Speak with them and learn about skills in the Ettenmoors.\n2\tPurchase and use the skill March!\tSovairlë instructed you to speak with them again and learn the skill March!. Then, you are to use the skill so that Sovairlë can see that you understand how to use the new skill you earned.\n3\tSpeak with Sovairlë\tYou successfully enabled the skill March!. Speak with Sovairlë again to learn more.\n4\tSpeak with Nadar near the gate of Gramsfoot\tYou have learned to strengthen yourself and to move swiftly. Sovairlë directed you to a vendor near the gate. Curious. Seek out the vendor Nadar and speak with them.\n",
[14000]="7001B9D8\n1\tTalk to Second-watcher Heathstraw\tSecond-watcher Heathstraw is just outside The Prancing Pony. He wishes to discuss his plan with you.\n2\tPurchase the Warrior Role Trait from Will, then talk to Tom to slot it, then use your skill to call forth your Warrior\tWill and Tom are outside of The Prancing Pony. They want to help you upgrade your soldier by allowing you to purchase and slot a role trait enabling him to be a warrior.\n3\tTalk to Second-watcher Heathstraw\tSecond-watcher Heathstraw is just outside The Prancing Pony. He wishes to discuss a few final details with you.\n4\tDefeat the first assault\tThe enemy is attacking The Prancing Pony. Aid Second-watcher Heathstraw in defending it.\n5\tTalk to Second-watcher Heathstraw\tSecond-watcher Heathstraw is just outside The Prancing Pony. He wishes to speak with you.\n6\tDefeat the second assault\tThe enemy is attacking The Prancing Pony. Aid Second-watcher Heathstraw in defending it.\n7\tTalk to Second-watcher Heathstraw\tSecond-watcher Heathstraw is just outside The Prancing Pony. He wishes to speak with you.\n8\tDefeat the final assault and Dríthlorz\tThe enemy is launching their final attack at The Prancing Pony. Help Second-watcher Heathstraw defend it.\n9\tTalk to Second-watcher Heathstraw\tSecond-watcher Heathstraw is just outside The Prancing Pony. He wishes to speak with you about today's success.\n",
[14001]="7006455F\n1\tArrive at Ost Ringdyr\tTravel out of Glân Vraig by the path along the cliffside to the east of Captain-General Tordúr and make your way to Ost Ringdyr.\n2\tUse the skill Return to Glân Vraig\tYou have discovered the keep of Ost Ringdyr. You should now use the skill Return to Glân Vraig to quickly return to the main encampment.\n3\tTalk to Captain-General Tordúr\tYou have returned to Glân Vraig. Speak with Captain-General Tordúr and let him know that you are prepared to fight in the battle for the Ettenmoors.\n",
[14002]="70064480\n1\tSuccessfully use Piercing Attack on training dummy Kelsen, Jalessa, or Light training-dummy Orion\030Successfully use Tainted Kiss on a target dummy\tYou are to go to the training dummies behind the totems in Gramsfoot and use your skills so that you might familiarize yourself with how to fight the enemy. Remember, you cannot attack or use skills while you are marching. You will need to disable the skill March! to begin attacking or use other skills.\n2\tReport back to Uglash\tYou have used both a ranged and a melee skill on a target dummy and should return to Uglash at Gramsfoot.\n",
[14003]="700644D5\n1\tSuccessfully use Lacerate on training dummy Kelsen, Jalessa, or Light training-dummy Orion\030Successfully use Hamstring on a target dummy\tYou are to go to the training dummies behind the totems in Gramsfoot and use your skills so that you might familiarize yourself with how to fight the enemy. Remember, you cannot attack or use skills while you are marching. You will need to disable the skill March! to begin attacking or use other skills.\n2\tReport back to Uglash\tYou have used two skills on a target dummy and should return to Uglash at Gramsfoot.\n",
[14004]="700644D7\n1\tSuccessfully use Strong Pull on training dummy Kelsen, Jalessa, or Light training-dummy Orion\030Successfully use Hindering Shot on a target dummy\tYou are to go to the training dummies behind the totems in Gramsfoot and use your skills so that you might familiarize yourself with how to fight the enemy. Remember, you cannot attack or use skills while you are marching. You will need to disable the skill March! to begin attacking or use other skills.\n2\tReport back to Uglash\tYou have used both a ranged and a melee skill on a target dummy and should return to Uglash at Gramsfoot.\n",
[14005]="700644D8\n1\tSuccessfully use Intimidating Shout on a target dummy\tYou are to go to the training dummies behind the totems in Gramsfoot and use your skills so that you might familiarize yourself with how to fight the enemy. Remember, you cannot attack or use skills while you are marching. You will need to disable the skill March! to begin attacking or use other skills.\n2\tSuccessfully use Cleave on training dummy Kelsen, Jalessa, or Light training-dummy Orion\tYou are to go to the training dummies behind the totems in Gramsfoot and use your skills so that you might familiarize yourself with how to fight the enemy. Remember, you cannot attack or use skills while you are marching. You will need to disable the skill March! to begin attacking or use other skills.\n3\tReport back to Uglash\tYou have used both a ranged and a melee skill on a target dummy and should return to Uglash at Gramsfoot.\n",
[14006]="700644DC\n1\tSuccessfully use Crippling Bite on training dummy Kelsen, Jalessa, or Light training-dummy Orion\030Successfully use Bestial Claws on a target dummy\tYou are to go to the training dummies behind the totems in Gramsfoot and use your skills so that you might familiarize yourself with how to fight the enemy. Remember, you cannot attack or use skills while you are marching. You will need to disable the skill March! to begin attacking or use other skills.\n2\tReport back to Uglash\tYou have used both a ranged and a melee skill on a target dummy and should return to Uglash at Gramsfoot.\n",
[14007]="700644DD\n1\tSuccessfully use Wisp of Acid on training dummy Kelsen, Jalessa, or Light training-dummy Orion\030Successfully use Acid-spike on a target dummy\tYou are to go to the training dummies behind the totems in Gramsfoot and use your skills so that you might familiarize yourself with how to fight the enemy. Remember, you cannot attack or use skills while you are Marching. You will need to disable the skill March! to begin attacking or using other skills.\n2\tReport back to Uglash\tYou have used two skills on a target dummy and should return to Uglash at Gramsfoot.\n",
[14008]="700644DE\n1\tSuccessfully use Fire Gourd on training dummy Kelsen, Jalessa, or Light training-dummy Orion\030Successfully use Headbreaker on a target dummy\tYou are to go to the training dummies behind the totems in Gramsfoot and use your skills so that you might familiarize yourself with how to fight the enemy. Remember, you cannot attack or use skills while you are marching. You will need to disable the skill March! to begin attacking or use other skills.\n2\tReport back to Uglash\tYou have used both a ranged and a melee skill on a target dummy and should return to Uglash at Gramsfoot.\n",
[14009]="7006447F\n1\tReturn to Akulhún for your newest orders\tUglash can prepare you for the fight to come no longer. He advised that you speak with the War-tyrant and begin your battles in the Ettenmoors.\n",
[14010]="7002615E\n1\tReturn to your trainers and learn how to improve your skills\tUglash has asked you to return to your trainers and learn more about what it takes to become a true soldier in the war against the Free Peoples. The trainers are back where you started your life as an Orc.\n2\tTalk to Ashrokil, the Corruptor of Gramsfoot\tHaving spoken with Dagalúr, you should now talk to the Corruptor to learn about traits.\n3\tTalk to Durglob\tNow that you have equipped some traits, speak with the corruptions trainer to learn more about corruptions in Monster Play.\n4\tTalk to Uglash to finish the tutorial\tNow that you have learned how to best equip yourself in Monster Play, speak with Uglash again for final instructions.\n",
[14011]="70064479\n1\tTalk to War-tyrant Akúlhun\tYou are directed to speak with War-tyrant Akulhún, the leader of the forces in Gramsfoot. He awaits you at the totems and bonfires down the hill near the exit into the Ettenmoors proper.\n",
[14012]="70064559\n1\tSpeak with the Medium Armour Quartermaster and learn about Audacity\tMake your way to the Medium Armour Quartermaster just to the west of Tordúr and purchase the gear you need to survive and thrive in the Ettenmoors.\n2\tTalk to Captain-General Tordúr\tNow that you are versed in the need for the gear that unlocks Audacity, return to Captain-General Tordúr.\n",
[14013]="7006455A\n1\tSpeak with the Light Armour Quartermaster and learn about Audacity\tMake your way to the Light Armour Quartermaster just to the west of Tordúr and purchase the gear you need to survive and thrive in the Ettenmoors.\n2\tTalk to Captain-General Tordúr\tNow that you are versed in the need for the gear that unlocks Audacity, return to Captain-General Tordúr.\n",
[14014]="7006455C\n1\tSpeak with the Heavy Armour Quartermaster and learn about Audacity\tMake your way to the Heavy Armour Quartermaster just to the west of Tordúr and purchase the gear you need to survive and thrive in the Ettenmoors.\n2\tTalk to Captain-General Tordúr\tNow that you are versed in the need for the gear that unlocks Audacity, return to Captain-General Tordúr.\n",
[14015]="70064473\n1\tReturn to your spawning den. Speak with Lenathron the Corruptor\tMalavin sent you back to where your journey in the Ettenmoors began to speak with Lenathron the corruptor.\n",
[14016]="70064476\n1\tReturn to your spawning den. Speak with Ashrokil the Corruptor.\tMalavan sent you back to where your journey in the Ettenmoors began to speak with Ashrokil the corruptor.\n",
